# {{ module_name }} JNI bridge

Generated by nexcpp. Java package: `{{ java_package }}`.

## Build the native library

```
mkdir build && cd build
cmake ..
cmake --build .
```

This produces `{{ module_name }}.dll` on Windows, `{{ module_name }}.so` on Linux,
or `{{ module_name }}.dylib` on macOS (no `lib` prefix — JNI loads it by the
bare module name).

## Compile and run the Java side

```
javac {{ module_name | capitalize }}.java
java -Djava.library.path=build {{ module_name | capitalize }}
```

Adjust the classpath if you place the generated `.java` inside its package
directory (`{{ java_package_path }}/`).
